{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":18775,"duration_api_ms":19840,"num_turns":6,"result":"I wrote the script to `src/cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`, but I haven't run it. My attempts to check the tracepoint and run bpftrace were blocked.\n\nIt hooks the `power:cpu_frequency` tracepoint. Each frequency change prints a line with the time, CPU, new MHz and previous MHz. On Ctrl-C it prints three per-CPU maps: the number of changes, a histogram of frequencies, and the average frequency.\n\nRun it with `sudo bpftrace src/cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`.\n\nIt only produces output if the kernel actually emits `cpu_frequency` events. Some drivers don't, such as `intel_pstate` in active mode and many VMs. If you see nothing, check `ls /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpufreq`.\n\nI can add a periodic `interval:s:1` sampler that reads the current frequency, or a `power:cpu_idle` view, if you want either.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a2e5f287-88de-43c1-9848-e535b3634105","total_cost_usd":0.07025034999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1941,"cache_read_input_tokens":128382,"output_tokens":1598,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1941},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":324,"cache_read_input_tokens":26428,"cache_creation_input_tokens":791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":791,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":351,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000451,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":12,"outputTokens":1598,"cacheReadInputTokens":128382,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1941,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.06979935,"contextWindow